                <tr id="issuerow12356675" rel="12356675" data-issuekey="IVY-67" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-67" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-67">IVY-67</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                resolver which always checks file system first
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> New Feature</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Xavier Hanin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Karl Baum
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Karl Baum
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 08/Aug/05 09:33 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 07/May/06 12:58 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 26/Nov/06 07:05 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.3            </td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    17/Nov/06
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      All
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      In a typical scenario, developers only store ivy files and artifacts on the local file system when they are unavailable from remote repositories.  The ivy resolver needs to handle the following cases:<br/>
<br/>
1) Ivy file on filesystem and artifact on remote repo.<br/>
2) Ivy file on remote ivy repo and artifact on file system.<br/>
3) Both Ivy file and artifact on filesystem.<br/>
4) Ivy file on remote ivy repo and artifact on remote repo. <br/>
<br/>
Currently this can be accomplished with a verbose resolver definition in the ivyconf.xml.<br/>
<br/>
http://www.jayasoft.org/node/207#comment-294<br/>
<br/>
Since this is a typical use case, I think it would be in ivy&#39;s best interest to come out of box with a resolver which handles this scenario.<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
