</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      linux 2.6.x, ant 1.6.3
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      Documentation for the chain resolver indicates that if the returnFirst attribute is not set, then Ivy will iterate through the chains selecting the *last* match. Either I&#39;m misunderstanding something or this is broken. To reproduce:<br/>
- create a chain resolver with two resolvers - a file system resolver and a url resolver.<br/>
- copy the repo from the url to the filesystem giving you 2 identical repos (except for timestamps)<br/>
<br/>
Perform a resolve - you should see that Ivy retrieves from the repo which is first in the chain.
  </td>
