                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows XP, Java 1.5, NetBeans 4.1 (5.0 beta), Ant 1.6.5
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      i&#39;am using ivy 1.2a with netbeans. Running the buildlist task works fine for the first time but after run once the task causes a NullPointerException.<br/>
<br/>
The reason is the following snippet from fr.jayasoft.ivy.ant.IvyTask:<br/>
<br/>
protected void ensureMessageInitialised() {<br/>
        if (!Message.isInitialised()) {<br/>
            Message.init(new AntMessageImpl(getProject()));<br/>
        }<br/>
}<br/>
<br/>
NetBeans starts Ant always within the same VM and fr.jayasoft.ivy.util.Message references statically an &quot;old&quot; Ant project. No buildlisteners are registered to the &quot;old&quot; project object anymore and so a call Project.log causes a NullPointerException.<br/>
<br/>
Please remove this static dependency because NetBeans + Ivy is really cool - when it works... :-)
  </td>
