                <tr id="issuerow12356701" rel="12356701" data-issuekey="IVY-93" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-93" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-93">IVY-93</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Ability to specify a root module in buildlist to filter out unnecessary build files
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Xavier Hanin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Kristian Cibulskis
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Kristian Cibulskis
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 19/Oct/05 12:10 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 21/Jan/06 15:32 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 26/Nov/06 07:03 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.3-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Ant            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    17/Nov/06
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      A discussion of this can be found at http://www.jayasoft.org/node/293<br/>
<br/>
Quoting the relevant section:<br/>
<br/>
We have the same problem here. Basically, we have a directory like:<br/>
<br/>
sandbox<br/>
-&gt; ComponentA<br/>
-&gt; ComponentB<br/>
-&gt; ComponentC<br/>
-&gt; etc.<br/>
<br/>
and components depend upon one another. Each component has an ivy file that defines it&#39;s dependencies. So say I have ComponentJ which depends upon H and C (and C depends upon A). What I have to do now is create a separate list of build.xml files for the buildlist target so that the build for ComponentJ only tries to order J, H, C and A. Otherwise I spend time building all the other components when they&#39;re not needed. Quite a pain because basically I&#39;m re-resolving what Ivy already knows about about the transitive dependencies.<br/>
<br/>
What would be great is if I could pass in the entire set of build.xmls for all the components and then say, effectively, &quot;Order this list of build.xml files as if I was building ComponentK&quot;. It would then order the entire list, and drop off all components (except the &#39;root&#39; one) upon which no other component was depending.<br/>
<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
