\ant\lib\junit-3.8.1.jar;.\ant\lib\xalan-2.5.1.jar;.\ant\lib\xsddoc-0.5.jar;
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      Look at the following  console output:<br/>
.maiden.retrieve.libs:<br/>
:: Ivy 1.2a - 20050916111245 :: http://ivy.jayasoft.org/ ::<br/>
:: configuring :: url = http://pinky/product-repository//ivyconf.xml<br/>
:: resolving dependencies :: wlpbp/javaframework-working@DEACW071<br/>
confs: [libs]<br/>
downloading http://ibiblio.org/maven2/xalan/xalan/2.5.1/xalan-2.5.1.jar ...<br/>
..........................................................................<br/>
.. (240kB)<br/>
[SUCCESSFUL ] apache/xalan-2.5.1/xalan.jar[jar] (602580ms)<br/>
<br/>
You can see:<br/>
=&gt; the download of xalan-2.5.1 needs 602580ms!<br/>
=&gt; the download of xalan-2.5.1 was flagged as successful, but you can see,<br/>
the jar size is only 240kB (normaly xalan has as size of 2840kB)<br/>
<br/>
If I try to download the xalan jar through my browser just in the time if ivy<br/>
wants to download it, my browser download runs, but not the ivy download.<br/>
As you can see in the  LOCALCLASSPATH I  use commons-httpclient.<br/>
<br/>
For me the bug is that Ivy doesn&#39;t realize, that a jar download<br/>
is not complete in case of a timeout or sth. else.<br/>
<br/>
See also forum node 347
