                <tr id="issuerow12356724" rel="12356724" data-issuekey="IVY-116" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-116" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-116">IVY-116</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Transitive Exclusions Not Working
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Xavier Hanin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Matt Inger
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Matt Inger
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 23/Dec/05 11:08 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 24/Jan/06 14:21 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 26/Nov/06 07:03 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.3-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.3-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    17/Nov/06
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Ant 1.6.5
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      I am having the following issue.<br/>
<br/>
Product A produces a war file, which resides in the &quot;war&quot; configuration<br/>
    &lt;conf name=&quot;war&quot; /&gt;<br/>
<br/>
    &lt;artifact name=&quot;A&quot; type=&quot;war&quot; conf=&quot;war&quot; /&gt;<br/>
<br/>
Product B produces a war and jar file, which reside in the &quot;war&quot; and &quot;runtime&quot; configurations<br/>
respectively.  <br/>
<br/>
    &lt;artifact name=&quot;B&quot; type=&quot;jar&quot; conf=&quot;runtime&quot; /&gt;<br/>
    &lt;artifact name=&quot;B&quot; type=&quot;war&quot; conf=&quot;war&quot; /&gt;<br/>
<br/>
The base build file merges any dependencies on &quot;war&quot; files into the web staging<br/>
area, before bulding the module&#39;s war file. Product B has a dependency on the war<br/>
file from module A.  As a result, the conents of A&#39;s war file, also end up in B&#39;s war file.<br/>
<br/>
   &lt;dependency name=&quot;A&quot; rev=&quot;&quot; /&gt;<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
Product C has a dependency only on the jar file of module A.  If I do this:<br/>
   &lt;dependency name=&quot;B&quot; rev=&quot;&quot; /&gt;<br/>
<br/>
I would, of course include B&#39;s war file into C&#39;s war file.  I would think any one of the following would<br/>
solve the problem:<br/>
<br/>
      &lt;dependency name=&quot;B&quot; rev=&quot;&quot;&gt;<br/>
          &lt;exclude name=&quot;B&quot; type=&quot;war&quot; /&gt;<br/>
      &lt;/dependency&gt;<br/>
<br/>
      &lt;dependency name=&quot;B&quot; rev=&quot;&quot;&gt;<br/>
          &lt;exclude name=&quot;B&quot; type=&quot;war&quot; /&gt;<br/>
          &lt;exclude name=&quot;A&quot; type=&quot;war&quot; /&gt;<br/>
      &lt;/dependency&gt;<br/>
<br/>
      &lt;dependency name=&quot;B&quot; rev=&quot;&quot;&gt;<br/>
          &lt;exclude type=&quot;war&quot; /&gt;<br/>
      &lt;/dependency&gt;<br/>
<br/>
      &lt;dependency name=&quot;B&quot; rev=&quot;&quot;&gt;<br/>
          &lt;exclude conf=&quot;war&quot; /&gt;<br/>
      &lt;/dependency&gt;<br/>
<br/>
      &lt;dependency name=&quot;B&quot; rev=&quot;&quot;&gt;<br/>
          &lt;include type=&quot;jar&quot; /&gt;<br/>
      &lt;/dependency&gt;<br/>
<br/>
However, it still picks up the war file from module A as a dependency, every time.  The only<br/>
way i&#39;ve seen to stop that from happening is the following;<br/>
<br/>
      &lt;dependency name=&quot;B&quot; rev=&quot;&quot; transitive=&quot;false&quot; /&gt;<br/>
<br/>
or<br/>
<br/>
      &lt;dependency name=&quot;B&quot; rev=&quot;&quot;&gt;<br/>
          &lt;conf name=&quot;war&quot; mapped=&quot;runtime&quot;&gt;<br/>
          ... Map out every configuration<br/>
      &lt;/dependency&gt;<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
It seems that if the &quot;war&quot; configuration from module B has a dependency on the &quot;war&quot;<br/>
configuration from module A, if you exclude all the artifacts from module B which fit<br/>
into the &quot;war&quot; configuration, it should exclude the artifacts as part of the dependencies.<br/>
<br/>
Any reason we can&#39;t just have a way to map a single configuration to something else, and<br/>
have all other configurations map to the same name?  In addition, I&#39;m not sure why you can&#39;t<br/>
specifically exclude a transitive dependency.  &lt;exclude&gt; seems only to work on direct<br/>
dependencies.<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
