                <tr id="issuerow12356747" rel="12356747" data-issuekey="IVY-139" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-139" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-139">IVY-139</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                possibility to configure ivy so that special revisions are not queried as fixed one at all
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Xavier Hanin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Xavier Hanin
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Xavier Hanin
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 18/Jan/06 14:55 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 23/Jan/06 15:27 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 26/Nov/06 07:03 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.3-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    17/Nov/06
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      For the moment when ivy tries to solve a revision, it first attempts with the revision as if it is a fixed one, and then if this fails check if it&#39;s a dynamic one and try to resolve it.<br/>
<br/>
Users using a lot of dynamic revisions suffer from this behaviour.<br/>
<br/>
Having the possibility to configure ivy so that this check is not done would be a good performance improvement in this case.
  </td>
