</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      For the moment when ivy resolve a dependency, it puts its ivy file in cache but modify it to store the information of which resolver was used to resolve it. This makes using the cache as a repository (with a mere copy for instance) not easy at all. Storing the resolver info outside the ivy file would let this task much easier.
