                <tr id="issuerow12356775" rel="12356775" data-issuekey="IVY-168" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-168" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-168">IVY-168</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Transitive Dependencies not evaluating properly
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Cannot Reproduce
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Xavier Hanin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Matt Inger
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Matt Inger
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 09/Feb/06 15:12 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 28/Aug/06 18:31 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 26/Nov/06 07:04 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.3-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.4-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    17/Nov/06
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I have configurations as follows in each of my modules within my org (fiberlink)<br/>
<br/>
&lt;configurations&gt;<br/>
    &lt;conf name=&quot;j2ee&quot; /&gt;<br/>
    &lt;conf name=&quot;compile&quot; /&gt;<br/>
    &lt;conf name=&quot;runtime&quot; extends=&quot;compile&quot; /&gt;<br/>
    &lt;conf name=&quot;test&quot; extends=&quot;runtime&quot; /&gt;<br/>
    &lt;conf name=&quot;war&quot; extends=&quot;runtime&quot; /&gt;<br/>
    &lt;conf name=&quot;tgz&quot; /&gt;<br/>
    &lt;conf name=&quot;provided&quot; extends=&quot;compile&quot; /&gt;<br/>
    &lt;conf name=&quot;default&quot; extends=&quot;runtime&quot; /&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/configurations&gt;<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
Assume that &quot;common&quot; has 0 artifacts included in the &quot;j2ee&quot; configuration.<br/>
If I have a dependency in moduleX on &quot;common&quot;:<br/>
<br/>
  &lt;dependency org=&quot;fiberlink&quot;<br/>
                            name=&quot;common&quot;<br/>
                            rev=&quot;&quot; /&gt;<br/>
<br/>
As, expected the &quot;j2ee&quot; configuration still has no artifacts (as<br/>
verified by the dependency report).  However,<br/>
If i then have moduleY depend on moduleX:<br/>
<br/>
  &lt;dependency org=&quot;fiberlink&quot;<br/>
                            name=&quot;moduleX&quot;<br/>
                            rev=&quot;&quot; /&gt;<br/>
<br/>
All of a sudden, the j2ee configuration has a whole bunch of jars<br/>
which should not be included.  I&#39;m not sure if it&#39;s getting confused<br/>
by the transitive dependencies or what, but it&#39;s not working right.<br/>
My current workaround is to put this on all my internal dependencies:<br/>
<br/>
  &lt;dependency org=&quot;fiberlink&quot;<br/>
                            name=&quot;moduleX&quot;<br/>
                            rev=&quot;&quot; conf=&quot;compile&quot; /&gt;<br/>
<br/>
so that only the compile configuration maps.  However, this is far<br/>
from the right solution, as I should really have all configurations<br/>
in my file moduleX to the correspondign configs in moduleY<br/>
(which i specify on the &lt;dependencies defaultconfmapping=&quot;*-&gt;@&quot; /&gt;<br/>
 element)<br/>
It&#39;s just that without the explicit mapping on the dependency<br/>
itself, it doesn&#39;t evaluate properly.<br/>

  </td>
