                <tr id="issuerow12356792" rel="12356792" data-issuekey="IVY-185" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-185" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-185">IVY-185</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                the ant task ivy retrieve does not work as expected using Netbeans 4.1 and mac os10.3
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Xavier Hanin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            faizal hussein
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            faizal hussein
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 05/Mar/06 16:40 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 06/Mar/06 12:17 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 26/Nov/06 07:05 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.2,                     1.3-RC2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.3-RC3            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Ant            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    17/Nov/06
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      mac os 10.3.9, ant1.6.2 jvm 1.4, netbeans 4.1
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      in the ant build.xml file a property is defined: &lt;property name=&quot;lib.dir&quot; value=&quot;lib&quot;/&gt; and later used by &lt;ivy:retrieve pattern=&quot;/[artifact]-[revision].[ext]&quot; /&gt;.<br/>
When the ant file is executed from the IDE, the files are retrieved into the path &quot;/lib/&quot; rather than to the project base dir. The expected behaviour is that the files will be retrieved to the /lib path. The behaviour is inconsistent with eclipse and invoking ant from the command line.<br/>
<br/>
A workaround is to define &lt;ivy:retrieve pattern=&quot;//[artifact]-[revision].[ext]&quot; /&gt;.<br/>
Note that the ant task mkdir resolves the  property correctly in Netbeans.<br/>
FYI Netbeans--&gt;Help--&gt;About--&gt;Detail shows that the current dir is set to &quot;/&quot;
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
