                <tr id="issuerow12356805" rel="12356805" data-issuekey="IVY-198" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-198" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-198">IVY-198</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                path separators in module names
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Xavier Hanin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Dan Weatbrook
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Dan Weatbrook
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 17/Mar/06 11:27 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 28/Aug/06 18:30 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 26/Nov/06 07:04 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.4-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    17/Nov/06
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      windows xp<br/>
ant 1.6.2<br/>
ivy 1.2a<br/>
jdk1.5.2_05
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      In order to support some organizational segregration,. We would like to be able to store our modules in a hierarchy, and refer to them by their location within the hierarchy.<br/>
<br/>
for example the we might want to name our modules like this<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
&lt;code&gt;<br/>
&lt;dependency  name=&quot;system1/applicationa/componentb&quot; rev=&quot;1.0+&quot;<br/>
&lt;/code&gt;<br/>
<br/>
it would then be located in the repository at <br/>
<br/>
&lt;code&gt;<br/>
repository\system1\applicationa\componentb\1.0.0\deliverables\comp-1.0.0.jar<br/>
repository\system1\applicationa\componentb\1.0.1\deliverables\comp-1.0.1.jar<br/>
&lt;/code&gt;<br/>
<br/>
This would seem like it should work, except that we are running into problems when ivy tries to create its cache files in the .ivy_cache directory by constructing the names like this <br/>
&lt;/code&gt;<br/>
.ivy_cahce\--.xml<br/>
&lt;/code&gt;<br/>
<br/>
using the above example it fails when attempting to create a file that looks like this<br/>
<br/>
&lt;/code&gt;<br/>
.ivy_cache\myorg-\system1\applicationa\componentb-default.xml<br/>
&lt;/code&gt;<br/>
<br/>
is the fact that this doesn&#39;t work a bug in ivy, something that we can configure, or are we just out of sync with the zen of ivy?<br/>

  </td>
