                <tr id="issuerow12356823" rel="12356823" data-issuekey="IVY-216" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-216" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-216">IVY-216</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Provide [keywords] as an alternative to wildcards in the configuration mappings
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Maarten Coene
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Maarten Coene
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 13/Apr/06 19:33 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 29/Feb/08 11:45 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.3.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    17/Nov/06
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Copied from http://www.jayasoft.org/node/589<br/>
<br/>
Having too many wildcard characters can be difficult to learn at first time, so being able to use either a more verbose keyword or a more synthetic wildcard seems to be a very good idea, which can be considered as an improvement request by itself.<br/>
We would thus have:<br/>
[this] = #<br/>
[all] = *<br/>
[self] = @<br/>
[other] = %<br/>
<br/>
Concerning backward compatiblity, using the brackets is a good idea cause there is few chance somebody used them before because it&#39;s the cahrracters used to identify tokens.<br/>

  </td>
