</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      If the revision is an empty string, the ModuleRevisionId encode/decode methods doesn&#39;t work:<br/>
<br/>
for instance,<br/>
ModuleRevisionId revId = new ModuleRevisionId(new ModuleId(&quot;J2EE&quot;, &quot;ejb&quot;), &quot;&quot;);<br/>
String encoded = revId.encodeToString();<br/>
ModuleRevisionId.decode(encoded);<br/>
<br/>
this will throw the following exception:<br/>
java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: badly encoded module revision id: &#39;J2EE:#@#:<br/>
ejb:#@#:&#39;<br/>
        at fr.jayasoft.ivy.ModuleRevisionId.decode(ModuleRevisionId.java:105)
  </td>
