                <tr id="issuerow12356843" rel="12356843" data-issuekey="IVY-236" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-236" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-236">IVY-236</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                ivy file &quot;artifact &quot; element &quot;conf&quot; attribute default behaviour does not match documentation
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Xavier Hanin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Matthew Cooper
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Matthew Cooper
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 27/Apr/06 18:08 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 28/Aug/06 18:25 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 26/Nov/06 07:04 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.3.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        1.4-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    17/Nov/06
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows XP
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      The documentation states that if the &#39;conf&#39; attribute is omitted from the &#39;artifact&#39; element (in the &#39;publications&#39; element) in an ivy file then it defaults to a value of &#39;default&#39;. The behaviour I see is that it defaults to &#39;*&#39;, i.e. all configurations. Looking at the code in fr.jayasoft.ivy.xml.XmlModuleDescriptorParser this seems to be confirmed:<br/>
<br/>
    public void endElement(String uri, String localName, String qName) throws SAXException {<br/>
        if (_state == PUB &amp;&amp; &quot;artifact&quot;.equals(qName) &amp;&amp; _artifact.getConfigurations().length == 0) {<br/>
            String[] confs = _md.getConfigurationsNames();<br/>
            for (int i = 0; i &lt; confs.length; i++) {<br/>
                _artifact.addConfiguration(confs[i]);<br/>
                _md.addArtifact(confs[i], _artifact);<br/>
            }<br/>
<br/>
which says that if we reach the end of the &#39;artifact&#39; element and have no configurations specified then add all the configurations defined in the ivy file.<br/>
<br/>
So either the code or the documentation is wrong.
  </td>
