</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        IVY-805                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Please please please please.<br/>
<br/>
Try to be consistent and avoiding funny names like &#39;allownomd&#39;. Any sane person reading that will wonder what this is.<br/>
This is annoying as you have in buildlist the attribute &quot;skipbuildwithoutivy&quot; where ivy is describing the &#39;module descriptor&#39;, so you have to make a choice of calling it either ivy either descriptor, but md is cryptic at best.<br/>
<br/>
why not something like descriptor=&quot;required|optional&quot; or ivy=&quot;required|optional&quot; ?<br/>
xml is not limited to boolean values<br/>

  </td>
