                <tr id="issuerow12356924" rel="12356924" data-issuekey="IVY-317" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-317" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-317">IVY-317</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Documentation of the deliver task
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Xavier Hanin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Antoine Sabot-Durand
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Antoine Sabot-Durand
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 04/Oct/06 14:53 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 06/Oct/06 16:56 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 26/Nov/06 07:05 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.4-RC2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    17/Nov/06
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      indifferent
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      I have had a look at the docu of the deliver task here : http://www.jayasoft.org/ivy/doc/use/deliver<br/>
<br/>
First comment is : in which use case is the direct use of this task needed in a build file. Does the publish task normally not do the work ?<br/>
<br/>
The main question is concerning recursive delivery.<br/>
<br/>
the table at the bottom says that recursive delivery is done by default.<br/>
<br/>
the description of the task at the beginning says &quot;..., and possibly do recursive delivery of dependencies&quot;.<br/>
<br/>
the paragraph titled &quot;do recursive delivery&quot; says &quot;this is done only if a deliver target is given to the deliver task&quot;.<br/>
<br/>
does recursive delivery work using ant ? does it call an ant target on each dependency of the ivy project ? this is not clear from reading the documentation.<br/>
If it uses ant - I suppose the &lt;ant/&gt; task, then which assumption does it makes about the name of the build files ? are they supposed to be called build.xml and to be each in the same directory as the ivy.xml ?<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
