                <tr id="issuerow12356947" rel="12356947" data-issuekey="IVY-340" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-340" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-340">IVY-340</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Ability to have multiple roots in the &lt;ivy:buildfilelist&gt; task
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Xavier Hanin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Matt Inger
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Matt Inger
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 10/Nov/06 18:06 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 16/Jun/08 17:25 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 06/Jan/07 11:52 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.4            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0.0-alpha-1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Ant            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    17/Nov/06
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      It would be extremely beneficial to have the ability to supply multiple roots in the &lt;ivy:buildfilelist&gt; task.<br/>
Support for instance, you have 10 applications in the same source tree, but only certain apps change<br/>
over a given development cycle.  It would be nice to be able to build only that set of apps and their<br/>
dependencies during the automated build. (Our build takes a property, and creates the buildfilelist<br/>
accordingly based on whether the property is set or not).<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
Right now, only 1 root can be specified:<br/>
<br/>
&lt;ivy:buildfilelist root=&quot;app1&quot; ... /&gt;<br/>
<br/>
i propose a comma seperated list (or any reasonable delimiter) to specify multiple roots:<br/>
<br/>
&lt;ivy:buildfilelist root=&quot;app1,app2&quot; ... /&gt;<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimespent"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="labels">    </td>
                                            <td class="customfield_12310220">            <span title="14/Nov/06 15:34"><time class="livestamp allow-future" datetime="2006-11-14T15:34:31+0000">14/Nov/06 3:34 PM</time></span>
    </td>
