                <tr id="issuerow12359764" rel="12359764" data-issuekey="IVY-372" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-372" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-372">IVY-372</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                ivyconf include syntax
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Gilles Scokart
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Eric Crahen
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Eric Crahen
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 04/Jan/07 05:30 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 13/Apr/08 19:00 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 13/Apr/08 19:00 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">1</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        IVY-387                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Any
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      It would be a handy thing if the &lt;include/&gt; tag within an ivyconf.xml could resolve files relative to the file requested, For example,<br/>
I might have a series of ivyconf files:<br/>
<br/>
http://www.myserver.com/ivy/ivyconf-default.xml<br/>
http://www.myserver.com/ivy/ivyconf-extras.xml<br/>
<br/>
The only difference between ivyconf-default and ivyconf-extras is that extras adds a different resolver. <br/>
If possible I&#39;d like to utilize all the stuff in ivyconf-default and not repeat that config in ivyconf-extras.<br/>
Ideally, ivyconf-extras would like sort of like this.<br/>
<br/>
&lt;ivyconf&gt;<br/>
<br/>
  &lt;include file=&quot;ivyconf-default.xml&quot;/&gt;<br/>
<br/>
  &lt;resolvers&gt;<br/>
    &lt;!-- New resolvers --&gt;<br/>
  &lt;resolvers/&gt;<br/>
<br/>
  &lt;!-- Additional property --&gt;<br/>
<br/>
&lt;/ivyconf&gt;<br/>
<br/>
Now when I ivy:configure url=&quot;http://www.myserver.com/ivy/ivyconf-extras.xml&quot;, what would <br/>
be nice would be for ivy to look at the include and say, I&#39;m going to resolve that against the<br/>
path of the config file I&#39;m processing, rather than resolve against the local filesystem; so it<br/>
would use http://www.myserver.com/ivy/ivyconf-default.xml from the remote server.<br/>
<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
