                <tr id="issuerow12360347" rel="12360347" data-issuekey="IVY-384" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-384" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-384">IVY-384</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Documentation menu unintuitive
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Won&#39;t Fix
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Gilles Scokart
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Gilles Scokart
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 12/Jan/07 08:04 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 25/Jun/08 10:58 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 25/Jun/08 10:58 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.4.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Documentation            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The documentation menu is a tree menu.   That natural and nice.  However, it&#39;s is quiet unexpected to have a page associated with the &#39;non leaf&#39; nodes.  It&#39;s also strange to see some leaf having no children.  The reader is asking himself &#39;why place this additional level&#39;.<br/>
<br/>
I think it should be better to have the intermediate nodes only used to expend (or collapse) the tree menu, and to move the page associated with the intermediate nodes to a leaf.  That would also accelarate the navigation to a low level leaf as no intermediate page will have to be loaded.
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
