</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        IVY-617                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      It seems that the ivy-report.xsl file still refers to various images at jayasoft and even though the URL is redirected to the incubator for ivy at apache, the images are not there either.<br/>
<br/>
The images in question are:<br/>
* http://ivy.jayasoft.org/images/searched.gif<br/>
* http://ivy.jayasoft.org/images/downloaded.gif<br/>
* http://ivy.jayasoft.org/images/evicted.gif<br/>
* http://ivy.jayasoft.org/images/error.gif<br/>
* http://ivy.jayasoft.org/logo.png<br/>
<br/>
Would it be possible to upload the images somewhere (or attach them to this issue) so I can download them and use a custom ivy-report.xsl. In addition, it would be good if the the ivy-report.xsl supplied with ivy refers to images that actually exist.<br/>
<br/>
It might also be a good idea to make the images part of the ivy project in subversion so they can all be kept together (or maybe they already are and I can&#39;t find them). 
  </td>
