                <tr id="issuerow12365487" rel="12365487" data-issuekey="IVY-443" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-443" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-443">IVY-443</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                order does matter in configuration extension when one is transitive and the other not
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            easyproglife
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            easyproglife
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 21/Mar/07 16:38 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 25/Jun/08 10:12 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.4.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I have &#39;compile&#39; and &#39;runtime&#39; configurations. &#39;compile&#39; is non-transitive and &#39;runtime&#39; is transitive.<br/>
<br/>
I have created &#39;both&#39; configuration that extends &#39;compile&#39; and &#39;runtime&#39;.<br/>
<br/>
I found it different if you define &#39;both&#39; in the following ways:<br/>
<br/>
1. &lt;conf name=&quot;both&quot; extends=&quot;compile, runtime&quot;/&gt;<br/>
2. &lt;conf name=&quot;both&quot; extends=&quot;runtime, compile&quot;/&gt;<br/>
<br/>
The first takes &#39;runtime&#39; artifacts non-transitively even thought it should be transitive.<br/>

  </td>
