                <tr id="issuerow12365806" rel="12365806" data-issuekey="IVY-449" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-449" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-449">IVY-449</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                buildnumber retrieves wrong ivy.revision - ignore status (milestone/release/integration)
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Daniel Schwager
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Daniel Schwager
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 26/Mar/07 11:40 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 24/Nov/09 22:39 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.4.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Ant            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        IVY-1121                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      WIndows, jdk 1.5.0.11, ivy1.4.1
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">          Hi,<br/>
<br/>
    i want to use use ivy:buildnumber to determine<br/>
    the next RELEASE-revision.<br/>
<br/>
    In my ivy-repository, i will find 3 version of mymod:<br/>
            1.2                     (release)<br/>
            1.3-dev20070326125300    (integration)<br/>
            1.3-RC1                 (milestone)<br/>
<br/>
    I want buildnumber to determine the next RELEASE, means 1.3.<br/>
    If i try<br/>
            &lt;ivy:buildnumber<br/>
                    organisation=&quot;myorg&quot;<br/>
                    module=&quot;mymod&quot;<br/>
                    revision=&quot;1.&quot; revSep=&quot;.&quot; defaultBuildNumber=&quot;1&quot;<br/>
                    prefix=&quot;base&quot;/&gt;<br/>
<br/>
    i get alway the revision 1.4. How can i tell the task to use<br/>
    only the &quot;latest.release&quot; as the searchbase ?<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
---------- &lt;Answer from mailinglist &gt;--------------------------------------<br/>
<br/>
I&#39;m afraid the buildnumber task cannot do what you want for the moment. Open a JIRA improvement if you want.<br/>
<br/>
For the moment, the only solution I see except writing your own task or patching the buildnumber task, is to separate your revisions in different repositories: one repository for releases, and another for milestones, and another for integration builds. Then you can use specific settings (ivyconf) to use only the release repo when you want to get your new release number. I don&#39;t know if it&#39;s possible in your case, but it&#39;s a good practice to separate them anyway.<br/>
<br/>
- Xavier<br/>
---------- &lt;/Answer from mailinglist &gt;--------------------------------------<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
Maybe a fix to the task: <br/>
- include the attribute &#39;status&#39; (like integration, milestone, release)<br/>

  </td>
