                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      IvyDE doesn&#39;t specify the ${basedir} property when resolving the dependencies.<br/>
This means that it&#39;s not possible to resolve jar files in a [project]/lib directory.<br/>
<br/>
For instance, the following resolver doesn&#39;t work:<br/>
<br/>
{code}<br/>
&lt;filesystem name=&quot;local-repository&quot;&gt;<br/>
      &lt;artifact pattern=&quot;${ivy.project.dir}/lib/[artifact](-[revision]).[ext]&quot; /&gt;<br/>
&lt;/filesystem&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
Maarten
  </td>
