                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        IVY-521                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      At the moment you have to disable validation when using extra attributes. There&#39;s already a suggestion to be able to configure the xsd to use in this case instead of disabling validation (IVY-521). Another suggestion is to activate namespace aware validation, extra attributes would be in different xml namespaces. The advantage is that upgrading Ivy version would be easier, the default validation would be used, only extra attributes would be defined and validated in separate xsd.
  </td>
