                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Currently it&#39;s possible to use poms with a filesystem resolver if you specify the pom extension in your &quot;ivy&quot; pattern, instead of using [ext]. However since all the AbstractResourceResolver subclasses can be m2compatible and hence basically maven2 aware, it makes sense to make any AbstractResourceResolver support usePoms.  It would also be more obvious than using the aforementioned ivy pattern.
