                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      When there is error (e.g. network error) when downloading the dependencies, Ivy should prompt the user the possible way to verify and try to rectify the error.<br/>
<br/>
Example when we encounter {color:red}&quot;Server access Error: No route to host: connect<br/>
url=http://repo1.maven.org/maven2/antlr/antlr/2.7.6/antlr-2.7.6.pom.sha1&quot;{color}, the user may be advised to<br/>
1) accessing the URL from the Internet browser and,<br/>
2) retrieving the file using wget<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
See also mailing-list subject:No route to host while resolving dependencies
