                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The attribute &quot;module&quot; has been used in &lt;info&gt; and &lt;exclude&gt; to indicate a module&#39;s name.<br/>
However, &lt;dependency&gt; uses attribute &quot;name&quot; to indicate a module&#39;s name.<br/>
<br/>
There are also attribute &quot;org&quot; and &quot;organisation&quot; found in some of the Ivy tags.<br/>
<br/>
We should standardise the attribute names.<br/>
<br/>
See also mailing-list, subject:Standardise the attribute names?
  </td>
