                <tr id="issuerow12373954" rel="12373954" data-issuekey="IVY-573" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-573" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-573">IVY-573</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Ivy causes IveDE to fail where a properties file is relative to ivyconf.xml
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            jamie burns
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            jamie burns
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 17/Jul/07 05:21 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 20/Jul/08 10:13 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 20/Jul/08 10:13 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.4.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        IVY-89,                                                IVY-387                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Eclipse 3.2, IvyDE 1.2.0, Ivy 1.4.1, Windows XP, Java 1.5.0_10
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      The issue manifests in IvyDE but lve confirmed it to be an Ivy issue. IvyDE fails to create a classpath container where ivyconf.xml has to resolve a properties file that is relative to ivyconf.xml. This occurs because Ivy only tries to resolve the properties file in the current directory. In the case of Eclipse+IvyDE the current directory is the eclipse.exe directory. So the following ivyconf.xml will cause IvyDE to fail.<br/>
<br/>
&lt;ivyconf&gt;<br/>
   ...<br/>
   &lt;properties file=&quot;local.properties&quot; ... /&gt;<br/>
   ...<br/>
&lt;/ivyconf&gt;<br/>
<br/>
(This will not fail if build.properties is in the same directory as eclipse.exe)<br/>
<br/>
I have created a patch which l hope l can attach to this issue.<br/>

  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
