</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      When Ivy is searching for a module in ivyrep, it already knows about the organization and module of a given file. It seems redundant to add them in the ivy.xml file. If they were optional attributes, it would be easier to add new modules. <br/>
<br/>
OTOH, adding a DTD/XML Schema would make it easier to browse than the docs.
