                <tr id="issuerow12378000" rel="12378000" data-issuekey="IVY-603" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-603" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-603">IVY-603</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Static revision replacement is not working when a dynamic revision is evicted by a transitive dependency.
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Xavier Hanin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Matthias Kilian
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Matthias Kilian
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 11/Sep/07 20:23 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 20/Sep/07 12:09 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 20/Sep/07 12:09 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        1.4.1,                     2.0.0-alpha-2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0.0-beta-1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Ant,                     Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">1</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      If A depends on B, rev=&quot;1+&quot; (which resolves to, say, A-1.2) and on C, rev=&quot;2.0&quot;, *and* C-2.0 depends on A, rev=&quot;2.2&quot;, i.e. if during resolution a dynamic dependency (A-1+ in this case) is evicted via a transitive dependency (A-2.2 via C-2.0), the delivered Ivy-file still contains the A-1+ dependency.<br/>
<br/>
This seems to be similar to IVY-404 and IVY-415, but maybe completely unrelated implementation-wise.<br/>
<br/>
I&#39;ll append testcases for both 1.4.x and trunk.
  </td>
