                <tr id="issuerow12381017" rel="12381017" data-issuekey="IVY-631" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-631" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-631">IVY-631</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Retrieval not expanding &quot;[originalname]&quot;
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Maarten Coene
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Anil Gangolli
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Anil Gangolli
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 23/Oct/07 22:14 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 08/Nov/07 02:31 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 05/Nov/07 10:21 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.0.0-alpha-2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0.0-beta-1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Ivy 2.0.0-alpha2-incubating<br/>
Ant 1.7.0<br/>
Sun JDK 1.5.0_12<br/>

  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      <br/>
I&#39;m using<br/>
<br/>
&lt;ivy:retrieve pattern=&quot;${deps.dir}/[conf]/[originalname].[ext]&quot; sync=&quot;true&quot;/&gt;<br/>
<br/>
With the following resolver definitions: <br/>
<br/>
  &lt;resolvers&gt;<br/>
    &lt;!-- We define two resolvers and chain them to form our normal resolver.<br/>
         The first is for thirdparty libraries, and the second is for libraries we build ourselves.<br/>
         The chain looks first in thirdparty libraries, and then in ours.  The first found is used. --&gt;<br/>
    &lt;filesystem name=&quot;thirdparty-libs&quot;&gt;<br/>
      &lt;ivy pattern=&quot;${top.dir}/thirdparty/libraries/[module](-[revision])/ivy.xml&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;!-- Patterns for thirdparty libs; in preferred resolution ordering. --&gt;<br/>
      &lt;artifact pattern=&quot;${top.dir}/thirdparty/libraries/[module]-[revision]/dist/[artifact]-[revision].[ext]&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;artifact pattern=&quot;${top.dir}/thirdparty/libraries/[module]-[revision]/dist/[artifact].[ext]&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;artifact pattern=&quot;${top.dir}/thirdparty/libraries/[module]/dist/[artifact].[ext]&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;!-- Also supported patterns: resolution of artifacts grouped by organization and module or only organization. --&gt;<br/>
      &lt;artifact pattern=&quot;${top.dir}/thirdparty/libraries/[organisation]/[module]/dist/[artifact].[ext]&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;artifact pattern=&quot;${top.dir}/thirdparty/libraries/[organisation]/dist/[artifact].[ext]&quot;/&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/filesystem&gt;<br/>
    &lt;!-- Workaround for JIRA IVY-630 --&gt;<br/>
    &lt;filesystem name=&quot;thirdparty-libs-no-ivy&quot;&gt;<br/>
      &lt;!-- Patterns for thirdparty libs; in preferred resolution ordering. --&gt;<br/>
      &lt;artifact pattern=&quot;${top.dir}/thirdparty/libraries/[module]-[revision]/dist/[artifact]-[revision].[ext]&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;artifact pattern=&quot;${top.dir}/thirdparty/libraries/[module]-[revision]/dist/[artifact].[ext]&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;artifact pattern=&quot;${top.dir}/thirdparty/libraries/[module]/dist/[artifact].[ext]&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;!-- Also supported patterns: resolution of artifacts grouped by organization and module or only organization. --&gt;<br/>
      &lt;artifact pattern=&quot;${top.dir}/thirdparty/libraries/[organisation]/[module]/dist/[artifact].[ext]&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;artifact pattern=&quot;${top.dir}/thirdparty/libraries/[organisation]/dist/[artifact].[ext]&quot;/&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/filesystem&gt;<br/>
    &lt;filesystem name=&quot;our-libs&quot;&gt;<br/>
      &lt;ivy pattern=&quot;${top.dir}/libraries/[module]/ivy.xml&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;!-- Ivy bug or lack of understanding: using optional revision (-[revision]) here doesn&#39;t work right.<br/>
           So we need two separate patterns. --&gt;<br/>
      &lt;artifact pattern=&quot;${top.dir}/libraries/[module]/build/dist/[organisation]-[artifact]-[revision].[ext]&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;artifact pattern=&quot;${top.dir}/libraries/[module]/build/dist/[organisation]-[artifact].[ext]&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;artifact pattern=&quot;${top.dir}/libraries/[module]/build/dist/[artifact]-[revision].[ext]&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;artifact pattern=&quot;${top.dir}/libraries/[module]/build/dist/[artifact].[ext]&quot;/&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/filesystem&gt;<br/>
    &lt;chain name=&quot;localtree&quot; returnFirst=&quot;true&quot;&gt;<br/>
      &lt;resolver ref=&quot;thirdparty-libs&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;resolver ref=&quot;thirdparty-libs-no-ivy&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;resolver ref=&quot;our-libs&quot;/&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/chain&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/resolvers&gt;<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
The behavior I am seeing is that whenever the artifact is resolved using the last resolver in this chain (the resolver named &quot;our-libs&quot; above) the artifact gets retrieved to the proper directory but with the name (verbatim) &quot;[originalname].jar&quot;, rather than the name with the appropriate value of &quot;[originalname]&quot; substituted in.<br/>
<br/>
This happens in 2.0.0-alpha2-incubating but was not occurring in 1.4.1<br/>

  </td>
