                <tr id="issuerow12381153" rel="12381153" data-issuekey="IVY-633" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-633" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-633">IVY-633</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Packaging Data Parsed Incorrectly in Maven 2 POM
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Maarten Coene
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Luke Majewski
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Luke Majewski
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 25/Oct/07 13:36 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 25/Sep/15 11:18 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 25/Jun/08 10:54 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.0.0-alpha-2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Maven Compatibility            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">2</td>
                                            <td class="watches">3</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        IVY-1534,                                                IVY-500,                                                IVY-799                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      There is still an issue with some dependencies whose extension is not specified in the default manner.  The example case is when trying to fetch some camel JARs.<br/>
<br/>
When trying to get the camel-script-1.2.0 JAR, you see:<br/>
<br/>
[ivy:retrieve]  ==== public: tried<br/>
[ivy:retrieve]    http://repo1.maven.org/maven2/org/apache/camel/camel-script/1.2.0/camel-script-1.2.0.bundle<br/>
<br/>
Ivy is trying to use the extension &quot;bundle&quot; and not JAR.  This is due to the code fetching the extension from the &lt;packaging&gt; element of the POM.  The relevant portion of the POM is here:<br/>
<br/>
&lt;parent&gt;<br/>
    &lt;groupId&gt;org.apache.camel&lt;/groupId&gt;<br/>
    &lt;artifactId&gt;camel-parent&lt;/artifactId&gt;<br/>
     &lt;version&gt;1.2.0&lt;/version&gt;<br/>
&lt;/parent&gt;<br/>
&lt;artifactId&gt;camel-script&lt;/artifactId&gt;<br/>
&lt;packaging&gt;bundle&lt;/packaging&gt;<br/>
&lt;name&gt;Camel :: Script&lt;/name&gt;<br/>
&lt;description&gt;Camel Script support&lt;/description&gt;<br/>
<br/>
Notice the &lt;packaging&gt;bundle&lt;/packaging&gt;.  Looking at the POM XSD it seems like this is a valid POM.
  </td>
