</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        IVY-514                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      While running a test with the latest trunk version of Ivy I noticed that the list of circular dependencies that Ivy had identified were displayed multiple times. For instance:<br/>
[ivy:resolve] 	circular dependency found: &lt;org&gt;#&lt;jar 1&gt;;working@&lt;machine&gt;-&gt;&lt;org&gt;#&lt;jar 2&gt;;latest.integration-&gt;&lt;org&gt;#&lt;jar 1&gt;;9.2.0.20071128125702<br/>
[ivy:resolve] 	circular dependency found: &lt;org&gt;#&lt;jar 1&gt;;working@&lt;machine&gt;-&gt;&lt;org&gt;#&lt;jar 2&gt;;latest.integration-&gt;&lt;org&gt;#&lt;jar 1&gt;;9.2.0.20071128125702<br/>
The display of entries could be added to a Set before printing to remove duplicates.<br/>

  </td>
