</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        IVY-665                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Ivy provides no help to clean a repository while keeping it consistent. Being able to delete a module revision and all its dependencies only if they have no depender remaining in the repository would be very useful to manage large integration repositories.<br/>
<br/>
This could be called with a dedicated task or triggered after each publish. Providing a flexible way to find the &quot;roots&quot; to delete (older than x, with more than y versions, ...) would also be very convenient.
  </td>
