                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      When a circular dependency is detected, the nodes in the loop are printed. The last node is printed as &quot;...&quot;. This way, we loose information, like which node is causing the problem. Therefor, it would be better if the last node was also printed (instead of &quot;...&quot;).<br/>
<br/>
cfr. IVY-672
