                <tr id="issuerow12384881" rel="12384881" data-issuekey="IVY-677" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-677" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-677">IVY-677</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                ivy:publish ignores error when ant runs with &quot;-quiet&quot;
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Henning Schmiedehausen
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Henning Schmiedehausen
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 18/Dec/07 15:54 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 22/Aug/08 15:47 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 22/Aug/08 15:47 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.0.0-beta-1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Ant            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Linux, JDK 1.4.2
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      I deploy artifacts into a repository using &lt;ivy:publish ... overwrite=&quot;false&quot;.<br/>
<br/>
When running a regular build using &quot;ant&quot; and I have already deployed an artifact, it reports correctly<br/>
<br/>
[ivy:publish] publish aborted: deleted /home/henning/....<br/>
<br/>
BUILD FAILED<br/>
... impossible to publish artifacts for myorg#mymodule;version: java.io.IOException: file copy not done from xxx to yyy: destination probably exists and overwrite is false.<br/>
<br/>
and echo $? (return code from ant) is 1.<br/>
<br/>
When I run &quot;ant -quiet&quot;:<br/>
<br/>
BUILD SUCCESSFUL<br/>
<br/>
and echo $? returns 0.<br/>
<br/>
Looks bad to me. If my build is not able to publish an artifact because I disallowed overwrite, this IMHO is a build failure and should not be ignored when running quiet.<br/>

