                                            <td class="votes">2</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        IVY-770                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows XP, Java 5
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      I&#39;m using &lt;ivy:makepom&gt; to generate pom files for a tarfile.  Even though ivy.xml declares the package type as &#39;tar&#39;, the makepom task sets the packaging type to &#39;jar&#39;:<br/>
<br/>
Input ivy.xml file fragment:<br/>
<br/>
    &lt;info organisation=&quot;myorg&quot; module=&quot;hello-package&quot; revision=&quot;1.0&quot;/&gt;<br/>
    &lt;publications&gt;<br/>
      &lt;artifact name=&quot;hello-package&quot; type=&quot;tar&quot; ext=&quot;tar&quot;/&gt;<br/>
      &lt;artifact name=&quot;hello-package&quot; type=&quot;pom&quot; ext=&quot;pom&quot;/&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/publications&gt;<br/>
<br/>
 Output pom file fragment:<br/>
<br/>
  &lt;groupId&gt;myorg&lt;/groupId&gt;<br/>
  &lt;artifactId&gt;hello-package&lt;/artifactId&gt;<br/>
  &lt;packaging&gt;jar&lt;/packaging&gt;<br/>
  &lt;version&gt;1.0&lt;/version&gt;<br/>
<br/>
Upon looking in the Ivy source, I found that the value is hardcoded in the method printModuleId in org.apache.ivy.plugins.parser.m2.PomModuleDescriptorWriter class:<br/>
out.println(&quot;  &lt;packaging&gt;jar&lt;/packaging&gt;&quot;); <br/>
<br/>
I did not see any easy way to fix this because it does not look like the type attribute is part of the module framework.<br/>

  </td>
