                <tr id="issuerow12389372" rel="12389372" data-issuekey="IVY-740" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-740" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-740">IVY-740</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Add a new resolve mode (optionally per module) to utilize new &quot;original constraint rule&quot; metadata in IVY-739
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> New Feature</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Xavier Hanin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Shawn Castrianni
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Shawn Castrianni
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 23/Feb/08 02:26 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 02/May/13 02:29 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 02/Mar/08 08:58 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        IVY-739                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      After IVY-739 is resolved, ivy will have new metadata that keeps the &quot;original constraint rule&quot; metadata in published/delivered ivy files.  Therefore, during a resolve, it would be nice to be able to use the original constraint rule instead of the specific revision it was published with by toggling on a new resolve mode.  Maybe this mode is toggled on via a new attribute on the resolve task, not sure.  But what is important is that this new resolve mode can be toggled on or off on a per module basis by a new attribute, perhaps &quot;resolveMode&quot; or &quot;mode&quot;, on the module tag in the settings file.  This would allow a specific module to always be resolved to the lastest version in the repo regardless of what was used to build the parent module that is referencing it.
  </td>
