                <tr id="issuerow12389373" rel="12389373" data-issuekey="IVY-741" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-741" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-741">IVY-741</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Enhance report task such that dependency graphs can show the original constraint rule on graph edges and resolved specific revision number on graph nodes
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> New Feature</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">    <em>Unassigned</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Shawn Castrianni
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Shawn Castrianni
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 23/Feb/08 02:29 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 02/May/13 02:29 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        IVY-739                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      After IVY-739 is resolved, ivy will have new metadata that keeps the &quot;original constraint rule&quot; metadata in published/delivered ivy files.  This can be used to enhance the report task.  Right now, if you run the report, you can see the dependency constraint rules for the direct dependencies of the module you are reporting on, but all of the indirect (transitive) dependencies are hardcoded to their specific resolved revision numbers.  Having this extra metadata could allow the report task to put the original dependency constraint rules on all the edges in the graph and the resolved specific revision numbers inside all of the nodes like it has now.  In my opinion, that is a better report of the dependencies of a module.  It shows the constraint rule used and the actual revision found for all nodes in the graph.<br/>

  </td>
