                <tr id="issuerow12389394" rel="12389394" data-issuekey="IVY-744" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-744" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-744">IVY-744</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Maven test scope not mapped to test conf
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Blocker
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Gilles Scokart
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Danno Ferrin
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Danno Ferrin
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 23/Feb/08 22:46 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 25/Feb/08 08:13 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 25/Feb/08 08:13 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.0.0-beta-2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0.0-beta-2            </td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The pom to ivy file translator incorrectly assigns the test scope of a dependency to the runtime conf in the ivy file.<br/>
<br/>
Consider the ivy beta-1 pom from http://mirrors.ibiblio.org/pub/mirrors/maven2/org/apache/ivy/ivy/2.0.0-beta1/ivy-2.0.0-beta1.pom<br/>
<br/>
the current parsed Ivy file is:<br/>
{code}<br/>
&lt;?xml version=&quot;1.0&quot; encoding=&quot;UTF-8&quot;?&gt;<br/>
&lt;ivy-module version=&quot;1.0&quot; xmlns:m=&quot;http://ant.apache.org/ivy/maven&quot;&gt;<br/>
	&lt;info organisation=&quot;org.apache.ivy&quot;<br/>
		module=&quot;ivy&quot;<br/>
		revision=&quot;2.0.0-beta1&quot;<br/>
		status=&quot;integration&quot;<br/>
		publication=&quot;20071213094244&quot;<br/>
	/&gt;<br/>
	&lt;configurations&gt;<br/>
		&lt;conf name=&quot;default&quot; visibility=&quot;public&quot; description=&quot;runtime dependencies and master artifact can be used with this conf&quot; extends=&quot;runtime,master&quot;/&gt;<br/>
		&lt;conf name=&quot;master&quot; visibility=&quot;public&quot; description=&quot;contains only the artifact published by this module itself, with no transitive dependencies&quot;/&gt;<br/>
		&lt;conf name=&quot;compile&quot; visibility=&quot;public&quot; description=&quot;this is the default scope, used if none is specified. Compile dependencies are available in all classpaths.&quot;/&gt;<br/>
		&lt;conf name=&quot;provided&quot; visibility=&quot;public&quot; description=&quot;this is much like compile, but indicates you expect the JDK or a container to provide it. It is only available on the compilation classpath, and is not transitive.&quot;/&gt;<br/>
		&lt;conf name=&quot;runtime&quot; visibility=&quot;public&quot; description=&quot;this scope indicates that the dependency is not required for compilation, but is for execution. It is in the runtime and test classpaths, but not the compile classpath.&quot; extends=&quot;compile&quot;/&gt;<br/>
		&lt;conf name=&quot;test&quot; visibility=&quot;private&quot; description=&quot;this scope indicates that the dependency is not required for normal use of the application, and is only available for the test compilation and execution phases.&quot; extends=&quot;runtime&quot;/&gt;<br/>
		&lt;conf name=&quot;system&quot; visibility=&quot;public&quot; description=&quot;this scope is similar to provided except that you have to provide the JAR which contains it explicitly. The artifact is always available and is not looked up in a repository.&quot;/&gt;<br/>
		&lt;conf name=&quot;optional&quot; visibility=&quot;public&quot; description=&quot;contains all optional dependencies&quot;/&gt;<br/>
	&lt;/configurations&gt;<br/>
	&lt;publications&gt;<br/>
		&lt;artifact name=&quot;ivy&quot; type=&quot;jar&quot; ext=&quot;jar&quot; conf=&quot;master&quot;/&gt;<br/>
	&lt;/publications&gt;<br/>
	&lt;dependencies&gt;<br/>
		&lt;dependency org=&quot;ant&quot; name=&quot;ant&quot; rev=&quot;1.6&quot; force=&quot;true&quot; conf=&quot;optional-&gt;compile(*),master(*)&quot;/&gt;<br/>
		&lt;dependency org=&quot;commons-httpclient&quot; name=&quot;commons-httpclient&quot; rev=&quot;3.0&quot; force=&quot;true&quot; conf=&quot;optional-&gt;compile(*),master(*)&quot;/&gt;<br/>
		&lt;dependency org=&quot;commons-cli&quot; name=&quot;commons-cli&quot; rev=&quot;1.0&quot; force=&quot;true&quot; conf=&quot;optional-&gt;compile(*),master(*)&quot;/&gt;<br/>
		&lt;dependency org=&quot;oro&quot; name=&quot;oro&quot; rev=&quot;2.0.8&quot; force=&quot;true&quot; conf=&quot;optional-&gt;compile(*),master(*)&quot;/&gt;<br/>
		&lt;dependency org=&quot;commons-vfs&quot; name=&quot;commons-vfs&quot; rev=&quot;1.0&quot; force=&quot;true&quot; conf=&quot;optional-&gt;compile(*),master(*)&quot;/&gt;<br/>
		&lt;dependency org=&quot;jsch&quot; name=&quot;jsch&quot; rev=&quot;0.1.25&quot; force=&quot;true&quot; conf=&quot;optional-&gt;compile(*),master(*)&quot;/&gt;<br/>
		&lt;dependency org=&quot;junit&quot; name=&quot;junit&quot; rev=&quot;3.8.2&quot; force=&quot;true&quot; conf=&quot;runtime-&gt;compile(*),runtime(*),master(*)&quot;/&gt;<br/>
		&lt;dependency org=&quot;commons-lang&quot; name=&quot;commons-lang&quot; rev=&quot;2.3&quot; force=&quot;true&quot; conf=&quot;runtime-&gt;compile(*),runtime(*),master(*)&quot;/&gt;<br/>
	&lt;/dependencies&gt;<br/>
&lt;/ivy-module&gt;<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
note that junit and commons-lang have runtime-&gt; when they should have test-&gt;<br/>
<br/>
patch forthcoming...
