                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      If a resolver references a cache that has not been previously defined, it should cause an error or at least a warning, but it does neither.  <br/>
For example, this should fail or warn because there is no cache &quot;bar&quot;.  It only prints an informational message that cache &quot;bar&quot; was assigned to resolver &quot;myfs&quot;.<br/>
<br/>
&lt;caches&gt;<br/>
  &lt;cache name=&quot;foo&quot;/&gt;<br/>
&lt;/caches&gt;<br/>
<br/>
&lt;resolvers&gt;<br/>
 &lt;filesystem name=&quot;myfs&quot; cache=&quot;bar&quot;&gt;<br/>
 ...<br/>
&lt;/resolvers&gt;
  </td>
