                <tr id="issuerow12391890" rel="12391890" data-issuekey="IVY-780" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-780" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-780">IVY-780</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                ivy properties defined in an include file not available in the file that includes it
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Xavier Hanin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Shawn Castrianni
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Shawn Castrianni
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 19/Mar/08 17:26 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 03/Apr/08 12:34 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 03/Apr/08 12:34 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">1</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Now that I check the code again, it seems that any property defined in an included file is not available in the file in which it has been included. As long as we have an history for the class (Jan 24, 2007) it has been like that. I&#39;m not sure why though, I see no added value in preventing included file to set properties in the including files.<br/>
<br/>
Do anybody see any reason behind this? Would it hurt to change that?<br/>
<br/>
Xavier<br/>

  </td>
