                <tr id="issuerow12391894" rel="12391894" data-issuekey="IVY-781" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-781" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-781">IVY-781</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                The retrieve task should allow to preserve directory structure reflected in organisation&#39;s dotted notation
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Maarten Coene
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Carlton Brown
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Carlton Brown
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 19/Mar/08 17:56 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 16/Apr/12 20:45 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 16/Apr/12 20:45 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.0.0-beta-2            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.3.0-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      For any publish-capable m2compatible resolver, &lt;ivy:publish&gt; will map dotted notation into a nested directory structure.   <br/>
<br/>
Currently, &lt;ivy:retrieve&gt; does not behave the same way.   When you retrieve an artifact with organisation org.ivy.foo, it retrieves into a directory named org.ivy.foo.   <br/>
<br/>
For consistency, it should map to a directory structure like org/ivy/foo the same way as &lt;ivy:publish&gt; does.   I think this should be the default behavior.   If someone decides they want it flattened, there could be an attribute flattenOrgNamespace or some such.<br/>
<br/>
This could be either a bug or an improvement, but I decided it was inconsistent and non-intuitive for publish and retrieve to handle dotted notation differently, so it could be considered a bug.  WDYT?
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
