</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        IVY-831                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Currently the &quot;ant coverage-report&quot; fails behind a proxy. <br/>
The reason is the forked {{&lt;junit&gt;}} task inside <br/>
{{ &lt;target name=&quot;test-internal&quot; depends=&quot;build-test, init-tests&quot; unless=&quot;skip.test&quot;&gt;}}<br/>
<br/>
It would be nice if the jvm proxy args (http.proxyHost http.proxyPort, etc; see http://ant.apache.org/manual/proxy.html) would be copied into the forked junit task. <br/>
<br/>
Then it would be possible to successfully run this task behind a proxy.
