                <tr id="issuerow12399783" rel="12399783" data-issuekey="IVY-857" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-857" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-857">IVY-857</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Better support for local builds
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> New Feature</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Xavier Hanin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Xavier Hanin
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Xavier Hanin
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 08/Jul/08 07:00 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 08/Jul/08 14:07 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 08/Jul/08 14:07 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.0-RC1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Currently Ivy suggests to use a local filesystem resolver in a chain with returnFirst=&quot;true&quot; to support local builds. It works well as long as you have control over the dependency revision requested, and can hence ask for a latest.integration version. But in some cases it would be nice to also override a transitive dependency, where do not control the requested revision.<br/>
<br/>
Eg:<br/>
#A -&gt; #B;1.0 -&gt; #C;1.0<br/>
A developer work on #A and #C, and want to use a local build for #C. But this requires a local publication of #B too, just too override the dependency on #C. It would be better to have a resolver able to force the returned module for the dependency on #C to a locally published module, whatever the requested revision is.
  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregateprogress">     
</td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimespent"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="aggregatetimeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="labels">    </td>
