</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The file property provided by the post-download-artifact trigger points to a file within the cache and not to the actually file in specified retrieve location. <br/>
<br/>
The description of the the trigger does not indicate if the file should already be in place however I believe this is a reasonable expectation. This would allow users of this trigger perform actions on the downloaded artifact. 
