                <tr id="issuerow12402196" rel="12402196" data-issuekey="IVY-881" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    Ivy
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="IVY-881" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IVY-881">IVY-881</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Ivy incorrectly searches for an artifact if it contains / in the name
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Resolved
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Invalid
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Xavier Hanin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Pavel Sher
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Pavel Sher
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 12/Aug/08 10:39 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 20/Oct/08 14:42 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 20/Oct/08 14:42 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Core            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">0</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Yesterday (2008-Aug-11) I&#39;ve build Ivy from the sources and found that Ivy cannot download artifact with / in its name. It seems the bug can be reproduced on windows only.  <br/>
<br/>
I have the following ivy.xml:<br/>
&lt;?xml version=&quot;1.0&quot; encoding=&quot;UTF-8&quot;?&gt;<br/>
&lt;ivy-module version=&quot;2.0&quot;&gt;<br/>
  &lt;info organisation=&quot;org&quot; module=&quot;module&quot; /&gt;<br/>
  &lt;dependencies&gt;<br/>
    &lt;dependency org=&quot;org&quot; name=&quot;dep&quot; rev=&quot;rev&quot; changing=&quot;true&quot;&gt;<br/>
      &lt;include name=&quot;dir/path-to-artifact&quot; type=&quot;zip&quot; ext=&quot;zip&quot; matcher=&quot;glob&quot; /&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/dependency&gt;<br/>
  &lt;/dependencies&gt;<br/>
&lt;/ivy-module&gt;<br/>
<br/>
I tried to debug Ivy source code, and it looks like the problem is somewhere near this code (IvyNode.java):<br/>
789:     Map allArtifacts = new HashMap();<br/>
                for (int i = 0; i &lt; confs.length; i++) {<br/>
                    Artifact[] arts = md.getArtifacts(confs[i]);<br/>
                    for (int j = 0; j &lt; arts.length; j++) {<br/>
                        allArtifacts.put(arts[j].getId().getArtifactId(), arts[j]);<br/>
                    }<br/>
                }<br/>
The produced Map of all artifacts contains dir\path-to-artifact instead of dir/path-to-artifact. And because of this matcher cannot find the required artifact. In Ivy-2.0-beta2 such artifacts were downloaded without problem.<br/>

  </td>
