                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      cywgin on MS Wondows.
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      A file name /path/to/repository is not absolute on MS-Windows.  A drive letter is needed.<br/>
<br/>
This is particularly confusing if using cygwin but is true when using Windows without cygwin (&quot;/&quot; is an acceptable path separator).<br/>
<br/>
Leads to less portability between Linux and Windows.<br/>
<br/>
In 2.0-RC-1, more paths must be absolute (e.g filesystem resolver artifact pattern, keyfile to sftp resolver).<br/>

  </td>
