                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Some maven pom license elements have a url element with a value which contains xml entities, for example &amp;amp;. When this is converted to ivy.xml, the xml entity is converted so that &amp;amp; becomes &amp;, and the ivy.xml cannot be parsed correctly afterwards. One example of this is http://mirrors.ibiblio.org/pub/mirrors/maven2/jboss/javassist/3.7.ga/javassist-3.7.ga.pom
