                                            <td class="description">      Overcome the temporary workaround where XML schema validation of Ivy files has been turned-off so Ivy extension attributes can be defined.<br/>
<br/>
&lt;ivy-module version=&quot;1.3&quot; xmlns:e=&quot;http://ant.apache.org/ivy/extra&quot;&gt;<br/>
&lt;info organisation=&quot;msjava&quot; module=&quot;tools&quot; revision=&quot;2.4&quot; e:jniPath=&quot;//ms/dist/msjava/PROJ/tools_jni/2.2//lib&quot;/&gt;<br/>
<br/>
Ivy lets you add custom meta-data where the meta-data property name is an xml value, not a validated part of the xml structure<br/>
<br/>
Improve Ivy xsd to handle the curent appraoch<br/>
o See info on xsd anyAttribute<br/>
o &lt;anyAttribute namespace=&quot;http://ant.apache.org/ivy/extra&quot;/&gt;<br/>
<br/>

