</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      After publishing an artifact to the repository. Ivy uploads an ivy.xml and generates related .md5 .sha1 files.<br/>
With a cleaned ivy cache the buildnumber task gives the wrong result when the ivy.xml in the repository is changed without changing the hash files.<br/>
This is ok, as there is at least a warning. But currently there is nothing. The ivy:buildnumber task runs without a message and returns the &quot;possibly&quot; wrong next revision.
  </td>
