                                            <td class="description">      Just as IVYDE-150, the documentation of Ivy can be added to the Eclipse Help center.<br/>
To not pollute the Ivy jar with some Eclipse specific resource, I think the best way to implement this is to have a seperate plugin: it would be basically just a jar containg a plugin.xml, the html files of the doc, and a toc file (toc file that can be generated from the xooki one).
